import ../../site/programs/controller.dl

set instance to an instance of dynlex website
set view to a new UI view
set view's instance to the address of instance
set state to a new website state
set state's view to the address of view
set instance's state to (the address of state) as a pointer
run website program 0 in (the address of state)
require condition ((the item at 0 in (state's programs))'s phase = 1) reporting "Run did not start compilation"
set reply to a JSON object containing [JSON number "status" is 0, JSON number "artifact" is 42, JSON number "milliseconds" is 0.5]
receive website compilation reply for 0 in (the address of state)
free reply
require condition ((the item at 0 in (state's programs))'s phase = 2) reporting "A successful compilation did not start execution"
set reply to a JSON object containing [JSON number "invocation" is 1, JSON text "output" is "64\n"]
receive website program output reply in (the address of state)
free reply
require condition ((the UI value for (the control labeled "Square field output" in (the address of instance)) in (the address of instance))'s text = "64\n") reporting "The output did not reach its named panel"
set reply to a JSON object containing [JSON number "milliseconds" is 0.25]
receive website execution reply for 0 in (the address of state)
free reply
require condition ((the item at 0 in (state's programs))'s phase = 0) reporting "Execution did not finish"
run website program 1 in (the address of state)
stop website program 1 in (the address of state)
require condition (state's requests' id = 2) reporting "Stopping did not remove the cancelled request"
run website program 0 in (the address of state)
stop website program 0 in (the address of state)
require condition (state's requests' cancelled) reporting "An already queued reply lost its ownership on cancellation"
set reply to a JSON object containing [JSON number "artifact" is 99]
discard website reply reply in (the address of state)
free reply
set pending to state's requests
loop while pending != @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to website request):
    set next to pending's next
    deallocate pending
    set pending to next
close the address of instance
print line "Website compilation, streaming output, Stop and queued-reply ownership work."
